      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen Image 2.1 - pose\n\n**What it does.** Puts a person into the pose of another photo. The pose picture is reduced to a stick figure (the pose skeleton), and the model draws the person along it. Only the pose is taken: nothing of the body, face, clothes or room of the pose picture comes along. See the note \"The pose picture\".\n\n**Use.**\n1. Load the photo with the pose in \"Pose picture\".\n2. Select \"Reference picture\", press Ctrl+B to switch it on, and load a normal picture of the person.\n3. Write the prompt and press Run.\n\n\"Pose skeleton the model follows\" shows the stick figure that was used.\n\n**Prompt.** Say who (\"the man from the reference picture\"), what to keep from them (face, hair, clothes), the pose in a few words as the pose picture shows it, then the place and the light. Do not describe positions in the frame.\n\n**Reference picture.** One slot, bypassed. The face must be large and clear in the reference picture. Without a reference picture the person comes from the prompt alone, or from a LoRA.\n\n**Variants.** Switch the two loaders and the ControlNet patch together:\n\n| Variant | Load Diffusion Model | Load Text Encoder | Load ControlNet patch |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| int8 | qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot | qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot | ..._fun_controlnet_union_int8_convrot |\n| nvfp4 | qwen_image_2.1_nvfp4 | qwen3vl_8b_nvfp4 | ..._fun_controlnet_union_int8_convrot |\n| bf16 | qwen_image_2.1_bf16 | qwen3vl_8b_bf16 | ..._fun_controlnet_union_bf16 |\n\n\"Load pose detection model\" (`sdpose_wholebody_fp16`) stays the same for all three.\n\n**Size.** The result takes the shape of the pose picture. \"Working size\" sets how large: 2 megapixels is saved (about Full HD). To get another shape, crop the pose picture first.\n\n**Strength.** On \"Apply ControlNet\": `strength` 0.8 and `end_percent` 0.7 are saved and tested. 1.0 with end 1.0 also works and holds the pose a little more strictly.\n\n**Skeleton options.** On \"Draw the pose skeleton\": body, hands, face and feet are on. Switching `draw_face` off leaves the head direction to the model; the tested result was just as good.\n\n**LoRA slots.** The three Load LoRA nodes are bypassed. To use one: select it, press Ctrl+B, pick the file.\n\n**Pictures per run.** `batch_size` on \"Empty Latent Image\".\n\n**cfg.** Keep 1. The negative prompt only has an effect above 1.\n"
      ]
    },
