      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "The pose picture",
      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## The pose picture\n\n**Only the pose is used.** The picture is turned into a stick figure: points for the joints of the body, the hands, the feet and the face, with lines between them. The person's body shape, clothes, glasses, face and the room are not passed on.\n\n**What makes a good pose picture.**\n\n- One person, whole body or the part you need, clearly visible.\n- Limbs not hidden behind objects or other people. A joint that cannot be seen is left out of the skeleton; the model then fills that part in freely.\n- Any size works: the picture is scaled for detection.\n\n**Check the skeleton.** \"Pose skeleton the model follows\" shows what was found. If limbs are missing or wrong there, the result will not follow them; use a clearer pose picture.\n\n**The result has the pose picture's shape**, and the person stands in the same place in the frame.\n\n**People only.** A skeleton exists only for human bodies. To keep the shape of an object, a room or a whole composition, use an edge (canny) control picture instead.\n\n**Several people.** The workflow is set up for one person. Detection of several people needs a bounding box per person and is not built in here.\n"
      ]
    },
